# JDBC thin 11.2 (ojdbc6) binding a CLOB and a BLOB OUT on 10.2.0.5 (#2803):
# `BEGIN SELECT c, b INTO :1, :2 FROM PYORACLE_TMP6 WHERE id = 1; END;`, behind
# a close-cursor piggyback; the LOBs' bind descriptors are those of the IN binds.
# Captured 2026-11-27 through tools/capture_proxy.py. The TTC payload,
# without the packet's header, as `hexdump -C` output; the offset column
# and the |ascii| gutter are ignored by tests.replay.parse_hexdump.
00000000  11 69 08 01 01 01 01 03  03 5e 09 02 04 29 00 01  |.i.......^...)..|
00000010  01 45 01 01 0d 00 00 00  00 02 7f f8 01 01 02 00  |.E..............|
00000020  00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00  01 42 45 47 49 4e 20 53  |.........BEGIN S|
00000030  45 4c 45 43 54 20 63 2c  20 62 20 49 4e 54 4f 20  |ELECT c, b INTO |
00000040  3a 31 20 2c 20 3a 32 20  20 46 52 4f 4d 20 50 59  |:1 , :2  FROM PY|
00000050  4f 52 41 43 4c 45 5f 54  4d 50 36 20 57 48 45 52  |ORACLE_TMP6 WHER|
00000060  45 20 69 64 20 3d 20 31  3b 20 45 4e 44 3b 01 01  |E id = 1; END;..|
00000070  01 01 00 00 00 00 00 00  00 00 00 00 00 70 03 00  |.............p..|
00000080  00 02 0f a0 00 00 00 00  02 03 69 01 00 71 03 00  |..........i..q..|
00000090  00 02 0f a0 00 00 00 00  02 03 69 01 00 07 00 00  |..........i.....|
000000a0
